WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.077
The authors follow prior work and evaluate on two
benchmarks.

00:00:04.157 --> 00:00:10.074
MNIST-scale is built by randomly downsampling MNIST
digits so that every resolution from

00:00:10.154 --> 00:00:15.049
eight-by-eight up to twenty-eight-by-twenty-eight
is equally represented.

00:00:15.129 --> 00:00:19.547
STL10-scale applies the same construction to
natural color images,

00:00:19.627 --> 00:00:23.431
spanning resolutions from forty-eight up to ninety-seven.

00:00:23.511 --> 00:00:26.702
They study performance under ideal downsampling,

00:00:26.782 --> 00:00:31.541
where theory exactly matches practice,
generalization to unseen scales,

00:00:31.621 --> 00:00:35.153
data efficiency at 5k, 2.5k, and 1k training samples,

00:00:35.233 --> 00:00:41.150
and a harder non-ideal downsampling setting where
the anti-aliasing filter is imperfect.
